1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,153
We start on the dashboard.

2
00:00:02,153 --> 00:00:07,784
Two things go wrong in every logistics business: stock that quietly disappears,

3
00:00:07,784 --> 00:00:11,847
and deliveries nobody can prove. Both are on this screen.

4
00:00:11,847 --> 00:00:16,480
What is below reorder level, and what is waiting to be confirmed.

5
00:00:17,300 --> 00:00:20,957
Inventory here is live, not a monthly spreadsheet.

6
00:00:20,957 --> 00:00:26,590
Every product carries its stock, its warehouse, and where it physically sits.

7
00:00:27,340 --> 00:00:32,991
Scan a label, and it answers the only question that matters on the floor.

8
00:00:32,991 --> 00:00:33,920
Which shelf.

9
00:00:35,540 --> 00:00:39,768
You can correct the shelf right here, and it saves instantly.

10
00:00:39,768 --> 00:00:43,580
So the next person does not walk the aisle for nothing.

11
00:00:44,330 --> 00:00:48,948
Goods arriving are recorded as a movement, not an overwrite.

12
00:00:48,948 --> 00:00:52,180
So every unit has a history you can trace.

13
00:00:53,130 --> 00:00:58,375
At month end, stocktaking compares what the system believes against what is

14
00:00:58,375 --> 00:01:03,760
actually on the shelf, and posts the gap as an adjustment. Not a silent edit.

15
00:01:04,530 --> 00:01:10,329
Now it ships. The office creates the dispatch, and assigns the driver.

16
00:01:10,329 --> 00:01:15,880
Only the office can assign. A driver cannot assign themselves work.

17
00:01:18,930 --> 00:01:20,575
The driver picks it up.

18
00:01:20,575 --> 00:01:25,295
When they arrive, they photograph the signed waybill on the phone.

19
00:01:25,295 --> 00:01:30,230
The consignee's signature, the date, the goods, captured at the door.

20
00:01:31,930 --> 00:01:35,106
And this is the part that changes everything.

21
00:01:35,106 --> 00:01:37,577
It does not count as delivered yet.

22
00:01:37,577 --> 00:01:40,964
The office gets a notification, opens the proof,

23
00:01:40,964 --> 00:01:44,070
and checks the photo before closing the run.

24
00:01:44,930 --> 00:01:51,990
Only then is it delivered. The driver's word is not the record. The photo is.

25
00:01:53,130 --> 00:01:58,140
Roles decide who can do what. A driver sees their own runs.

26
00:01:58,140 --> 00:02:02,470
Only an owner assigns work, or confirms a delivery.

27
00:02:03,230 --> 00:02:06,279
And every action is logged against a name.

28
00:02:06,279 --> 00:02:09,690
That is what accounted for actually looks like.
